   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Pets and the farm",
     "texto": [
      "To say which animal you have, use **tener**:\n\n- Tengo **un perro**.\n- Mis abuelos **tienen** una granja con vacas y caballos.\n\nAnd to say what you like, the verb **gustar** works the other way round:\n\n- **Me gustan** los gatos. (los gatos is the subject)\n- **Me encantan** los perros. (even stronger)\n\nNote: «me gusta» goes with one animal in the singular and «me gustan» with several."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Gustar, encantar and tener miedo",
     "texto": [
      "**Gustar** and **encantar** work the same way, and the subject is the animal or thing that is liked:\n\n- **Me gusta** el perro. → singular\n- **Me gustan** los perros. → plural\n- **Me encantan** los gatos. → more intense\n\nTo ask: **¿Te gustan los animales?**\n\nAnd fear goes with **tener miedo de**: «Tengo miedo **de** los caballos». Always with «de»."
     ],
     "ejemplos": [
      {
       "quien": {
        "texto": "",
        "lengua": "alumno"
       },
       "estudio": "Me gustan los gatos.",
       "alumno": "I like cats.",
       "literal": "",
       "estructura": "",
       "nota": [],
       "analisis": [
        [
         "Me gustan",
         "predicate"
        ],
        [
         "Me",
